      },
      "description": "Current reviewed ruleset 59752c1132f0; historical rulesets remain queryable in Loki. Controlled tests and expected activity are not automatically attacks."
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "title": "Recent Runtime Security Events",
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{app=\"platform-falco\",runtime_ruleset=\"59752c1132f0\"} | json | __error__=\"\" | source=\"syscall\" | rule=~\"Platform Runtime .*\"",
          "queryType": "range",
          "legendFormat": "{{rule}} {{output_fields_k8s_ns_name}} {{output_fields_k8s_pod_name}} {{node}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Current reviewed ruleset 59752c1132f0; historical rulesets remain queryable in Loki. Controlled tests and expected activity are not automatically attacks."
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Runtime interpretation and coverage",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 62,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Falco is detection, not a blocker. Kyverno Enforce remains scoped to devsecops-execution; production candidate auditing is separate. Trivy scans image vulnerabilities.\n\nCoverage: devops ARM64 node only; monitored namespaces petclinic and devsecops-test. Cloud workers are not covered.\n\nFalco priorities have no High value: the severe panel maps Error/Critical/Alert/Emergency explicitly. Notice curl/wget execution is visibility, not automatically an attack. Test events and expected operator activity remain visible. No automatic containment is enabled.\n\nBusiness panels select reviewed ruleset 59752c1132f0. Earlier versions remain in {app=\"platform-falco\"}. The separate sensor diagnostics panel includes historical internal drop reports across all versions; no reports is not proof of lossless capture."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "title": "Falco sensor diagnostics — internal drop reports (all versions)",
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 54,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{app=\"platform-falco\"} | json | __error__=\"\" | rule=\"Falco internal: syscall event drop\"",
          "queryType": "range",
          "legendFormat": "{{rule}} {{output_fields_k8s_ns_name}} {{output_fields_k8s_pod_name}} {{node}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Historical per-process startup drop reports remain visible. Empty window means no received reports, not a lossless-capture guarantee. Inspect Prometheus counters and process lifecycle separately."
    }
  ]
}
